schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Localism Fund launched with $155,000 in pooled initial funding
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    The Localism Fund, stewarded through Regen Coordination (the joint effort
    of ReFi DAO and Greenpill Network) and OpenCivics, launched with $155,000
    in initial funding from Gitcoin, Celo Public Goods, Ma Earth, and the
    Ethereum Foundation, with the stated purpose of helping place-based groups
    run their own grant programs without extracting from them.
  evidence: >-
    Cited to "Introducing the Localism Fund" (blog.refidao.com) in the
    article's References.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/what-is-local-node.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the article's clearest, most concrete example of the network
    pooling capital and routing it down to local groups — presented as
    reassurance against the fear that node-level funding requires competing
    alone.
  uncertainty: >-
    Single-source figure (the fund's own launch announcement); no independent
    verification of the dollar amount or funder list in this article, and no
    date given for how current the $155,000 figure remains as the fund
    disburses over time.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/what-is-local-node.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
